    The response is superlinear in gust intensity. DO NOT read that
    as aerodynamic nonlinearity: `aero.py` is linear in alpha and
    the entry flown here carries no CL table. The drift line above
    is the candidate -- with fixed controls and nobody flying, the
    aeroplane leaves the condition it was trimmed for, and dynamic
    pressure changes with it. Attributed, not merely noted.

